hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"296","On crucifixion: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Abu al-Haytham narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crucified Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt to a tree. He said: O Messenger of Allah, am I (singled out) apart from Quraysh? He said: Yes. He said: Then who will care for the children? He said: The Fire."
"297","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from al-Hasan, he said: The idolaters offered ounces of gold to a man to kill the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized him and crucified him on a mountain in Madinah called Dhubab; he was the first one crucified in Islam."
